# What an Android app's own library has to expose to anything outside itself.
#
# `libP44.so` exported 151,047 symbols and needed 31. The other 151,016 are the
# public API of SwiftCrossUI, AndroidBackend, SwiftJava and libwebp, which are
# statically linked into it and have no consumer outside it: measured on the
# 2026-09-05 release APK, .dynstr 11.06 MB + .dynsym 3.49 MB + .gnu.hash
# 0.97 MB + .gnu.version 0.29 MB = 15.81 MB, or 34% of a 46.4 MB library, for
# names nothing looks up. Swift mangling is why the string table is three times
# the symbol table: the mean exported name is 76 characters and the longest is
# 617.
#
# Everything on the global list has an actual caller across a .so boundary, and
# each was checked rather than assumed:
#
#   AndroidBackend_entrypoint  libshim.so holds the one undefined reference to
#                              it -- `llvm-nm -D --undefined-only` on every
#                              library in the APK finds exactly that one. It is
#                              the @_cdecl in AndroidBackend.swift.
#   Java_*, JNI_OnLoad         resolved by the JVM by name at registration
#                              time, which is a lookup no linker can see.
#                              JNI_OnUnload was listed here too, from the JNI
#                              convention rather than from the symbol table,
#                              and the link failed with "version script
#                              assignment of 'global' to symbol 'JNI_OnUnload'
#                              failed: symbol not defined". Swift's runtime
#                              does not define one. lld only raises this for a
#                              literal name -- a pattern like Java_* matching
#                              nothing is silent -- so the list above is
#                              exactly the set that was read out of
#                              `llvm-nm -D --defined-only`.
#   main                       called from the entrypoint in the same library,
#                              so it does not need to be here; kept because an
#                              exported `main` is what the platform expects of
#                              a library that has one.
#
# `local: *` is the part that saves the space, and it is also the part that
# could break something: hiding a symbol means a second copy of it elsewhere no
# longer coalesces with this one. Verified rather than reasoned about -- see
# testapp/README.md for which apps were run and what was compared.
#
# 一個 Android app 自己的 library 必須向外界暴露的東西。
#
# `libP44.so` 匯出了 151,047 個符號，而它需要的是 31 個。其餘 151,016 個是 SwiftCrossUI、
# AndroidBackend、SwiftJava 與 libwebp 的 public API——它們被靜態連結進來，在該 library 之外
# 沒有任何消費者：以 2026-09-05 的 release APK 實測，.dynstr 11.06 MB + .dynsym 3.49 MB +
# .gnu.hash 0.97 MB + .gnu.version 0.29 MB = 15.81 MB，佔一個 46.4 MB library 的 34%，
# 而那些名字沒有任何東西會去查。字串表是符號表的三倍，原因是 Swift 的名稱修飾：匯出名稱平均
# 76 個字元，最長的一個是 617 個。
#
# global 清單上的每一項都有跨 .so 的真實呼叫者，且每一項都是查證而非假設得來的：
#
#   AndroidBackend_entrypoint  對它的唯一未定義參考在 libshim.so——對 APK 中每一個 library
#                              執行 `llvm-nm -D --undefined-only` 恰好找到那一個。它就是
#                              AndroidBackend.swift 中的那個 @_cdecl。
#   Java_*、JNI_OnLoad         由 JVM 在註冊時以名稱解析，那是任何 linker 都看不見的查找。
#                              此處原本還列了 JNI_OnUnload——那是依 JNI 慣例寫的，不是從符號表
#                              讀來的——連結因而失敗，訊息為「version script assignment of
#                              'global' to symbol 'JNI_OnUnload' failed: symbol not defined」。
#                              Swift 的 runtime 並未定義它。lld 只對「字面名稱」發出此錯誤
#                              ——像 Java_* 這種一個都沒配對到的樣式是沉默的——因此上方清單
#                              恰好就是從 `llvm-nm -D --defined-only` 讀出來的那一組。
#   main                       由同一個 library 中的 entrypoint 呼叫，因此並不需要列在此處；
#                              保留它，是因為一個帶有 main 的 library 被平台預期會匯出它。
#
# `local: *` 是省下空間的那一部分，也是可能弄壞東西的那一部分：隱藏一個符號，意味著別處的第二份
# 副本不再與這一份合併。此事以驗證確認，而非以推理斷定——跑了哪些 app、比對了什麼，見
# testapp/README.md。
{
  global:
    AndroidBackend_entrypoint;
    JNI_OnLoad;
    Java_*;
    main;

  local:
    *;
};
